In fact, the 35 mm format can be somewhat misleading, as it has a width of 36 millimeters and a height of 24 millimeters.
Therefore, the ratio of the dimensions of this format (which we divide by twelve to obtain the simplest ratio with whole numbers) is expressed as 3:2.
Many common formats (such as the APS family formats) have an aspect ratio equal to or very close to this.
