Christmas is one of the most important holidays in Christianity and is celebrated as the birthday of Jesus Christ.
Many of these holiday traditions have also been adopted by people in Christian countries who do not adhere to this religion, as well as by non-Christians around the world.
There is a tradition of staying awake on the night of Eid al-Fitr in places that are visible, so that one can witness the sunrise.
Certainly, Christianity has religious explanations for this tradition, but it can well be said that it may have originally been a celebration of spring and fertility prior to the advent of Christianity.
Most traditional churches usually hold the Easter Vigil on Saturday night during the Easter holiday, while this congregation often gathers at midnight to celebrate Christ's Resurrection.
All animals that initially reached the islands came here either by swimming, flying, or floating.
Due to the great distance from the mainland, mammalian animals were unable to reach there, so the large turtle is the primary animal that grazes in the Galápagos.
Since humans arrived in the Galápagos, many mammals have been introduced to the islands, including goats, horses, cattle, mice, cats, and dogs.
If you visit the North or South Pole during winter, you will witness the polar night, meaning the sun never rises above the horizon.
This provides a good opportunity to see the aurora borealis, as the sky will be mostly dark throughout the day and night.
Since these areas are sparsely populated and, for this very reason, light pollution is not an issue, you can also enjoy the stars.
Japanese work culture is more hierarchical and formal than what Westerners are accustomed to.
The clothes are standard work attire, and colleagues address each other by their surnames or job titles.
Cooperation in the workplace is very important, and instead of praising individual achievements, emphasis should be placed on group effort.
Workers must often obtain their bosses' approval for every decision they make, and they are expected to obey their bosses' instructions without question.
